*HEADING
A 1 x 1 x 2 block of C3D20R bricks clamped at its base, an oblique surface traction
(*DSLOAD TRVEC) on its top face, whose nodes carry local axes: a rectangular *TRANSFORM
on one half of the face and a cylindrical one (skew axis outside the block) on the other.
A *CLOAD on such a node acts in its local axes (Abaqus and ccx alike), so the traction's
nodal forces must be given in them: the displacements match the same block without
any *TRANSFORM (validate_with_ccx.py).
** node (i, j, k) = 1 + i + 10 j + 100 k: i, j = 0..4 across, k = 0..8 up the block
*NODE
